# selection-world
#
# Operator selection by look-ahead. When operators tie, an evaluation substate applies each candidate (in a copy 
# of the state) and compares the outcomes; the project supplies the evaluation machinery and the strategies that 
# decide how deep and how to prefer outcomes. Task independent: it only needs ^desireds on the state and task 
# operators marked ^task-operator.
#
# Requires: soar-base.
# Loaded by: soar-library.soar
#
# Contents (rules per file)
#      3  _flags.soar: Defaults for the flags the selection rules read (verify, guardrails, hierarchical-properties).
#     30  Operator_Tie/elaborations.soar: Selection problem space: creating evaluation operators for tied operators, comparing evaluations (success > partial success > ...), turning evaluations into preferences.
#      7  Operator_Tie/evaluate-operator.soar: The evaluate-operator operator: proposed per tied operator, creates the evaluation when selected.
#      1  Operator_Tie/Impasse__State_No-Change/elaborations.soar: Conflict rejection in the selection space (default*select*reject*conflict).
#     37  Operator_Tie/evaluate-operator/elaborations.soar: Evaluation substate: copies the state, desireds and world into the substate, applies the evaluated operator, detects success/failure and reports it.
#      1  Operator_Tie/evaluate-operator/task-operator.soar: Applying the task operator being evaluated inside the evaluation substate.
#      1  Operator_Tie/evaluate-operator/Operator_Constraint-Failure/elaborations.soar
#      2  Operator_Tie/evaluate-operator/Operator_Tie/elaborations.soar
#      1  Operator_Tie/evaluate-operator/State_No-Change/elaborations.soar
#      1  Operator_Tie/evaluate-operator/State_No-Change/State_No-Change/elaborations.soar
#      3  elaborations/top-state.soar: Halting the top-level goal with success or failure (top-goal*halt*...), including the desireds-count test.
#    94  strategies/: Strategies for how look-ahead proceeds and how outcomes are preferred (see below).
#
# Strategies: strategies/strategies_source.soar sources iterative-deepening and first-success. strategies/optimal was retired in v2.15;
# cost-aware selection uses the agent-world flags cost-metric (none|unit|time) and the selection-world flag optimize (false|true).
#
# Datamap
#   selection-world.vsa.json holds this project's state attributes plus those of the projects it requires.
#   Top-state attributes owned by this project: ^constants, ^current-evaluation-depth, ^depth, ^desireds, ^duplicate-look-ahead-operator, ^duplicate-of, ^evaluation, ^exhaustion-failure, ^flag-override, ^flags, ^internal-actions, ^look-ahead-operator, ^minimum-numeric-value, ^numeric-value, ^problem-space, ^prohibit-failure, ^real, ^required-success, ^selection-superstate, ^success, ^tried-tied-operator, ^type, ^verbose, ^world
#   Single source: datamaps/library-datamap.json (each edge tagged with its owning project). Regenerate the
#   project files with: python3 tools/datamaps.py <this-directory> --assemble
#
# Flags read: aspiration, aspiration-step, progress-score, progress-threshold, termination, cost-quantum, guardrails, hierarchical-properties, init-evaluation-depth, iterative-step (operator | tie-impasse | cost), optimize, verify
# Flags written: (none recorded)
# Hooks: not yet defined (see the refactoring proposal, Section 4); this file will list them.
# Conventions: every rule is :default; no rule name is defined twice among the sourced files; do not excise rules to override them.
# Notes: docs/ holds comment-only notes from the old projects (not sourced).

